    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d78-a3">

                <pb facs="0200" n="106" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg106"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tillman to
                        General Alfaro.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States.</hi><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-02-29"><hi rendition="#italic">February 29,
                        1896.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In view of a telegram received to-day from
                    my Government, expressing satisfaction with Mr. St. John as arbitrator on the
                    Santos claim, I beg leave to call your attention to my communication of February
                    16, and again respectfully ask if Mr. St. John is acceptable to the Government
                    of Ecuador?</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James D. Tillman.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
